  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Although Egypt has suffered less than other countries from the economic and social impact of the global COVID-19 pandemic, it is clear that employment challenges have worsened, especially for youth and women, with an increase in informal and irregular forms of work. Throughout this biennum, the Egyptian Government began the process of modifying national labour law no.12 for 2003, and initiated the development of two vital interlinked strategies, namely, the National Employment Strategy (NES), and the National Strategy on Formalisation. Furthermore, a new decree is being discussed on the development of &#x201c;National Council for Consultation&#x201d; replacing the National council for Social Dialogue. It is very curial that Worker&#x2019;s organisations are capacitated to be able to influence these legislations and strategies including integrating just transition as an approach to address unemployment challenges through a comprehensive intervention model that links between indicators 2.2.1 and 2.2.2, to ensure increase representation from diversified workers group, specifically from those affected by climate change, and worker&#x2019;s organisation&#x2019;s ability to influence policies, and ensure application of international labour standards.</narrative>
  </description>
